      "writtenOn": "2015-05-12T23:09:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The new system consistently uses \"device\" to refer to device-side code, and uses \"target\" the way gcc or clang does - to select what environment you are targeting.  \"os\" is not sufficient, because we use it to differentiate host vs. android as well as linux vs. darwin vs. windows and android_arm vs. android_x86, etc.\n\nIn any case, this is just rearranging the code to make the \"not_\" explicit instead of magical, any renames would be a separate patch.",
